msgid "文字 Panic 诊断"
msgstr "Text Panic Diagnostics"

msgid "输出行为"
msgstr "Output Behavior"

msgid ""
"文本 VT 保留编号并从当前位置继续输出；GUI 从屏幕左上角绘制文字。 只有文字及空格占用的字符格覆盖黑底，其余 framebuffer 像素保持原样。 GUI "
"到达底部停止可见绘制，不滚动原桌面；完整诊断继续进入串口和 VT 历史。 红色标题、黄色解释及白色寄存器提高可读性，控制字符受限并转义。"
msgstr ""
"A text VT retains its number and continues output from the current position; in a GUI, text is "
"drawn from the top-left corner. Only character cells occupied by text or spaces are covered with a"
" black background; other framebuffer pixels are left intact. GUI drawing stops visibly at the "
"bottom without scrolling the original desktop; full diagnostics continue to the serial port and VT"
" history. A red heading, yellow explanation, and white registers improve readability, with control"
" characters restricted and escaped."

msgid ""
"诊断包括异常与错误码、RIP/RSP/RFLAGS、段/控制寄存器、页错误解释、可用的 通用寄存器、CPU/APIC、其他 CPU 停机数量、任务/PID、内核版本与构建身份。 "
"入口未保存的值明确标为不可用，不把过期 CR2 解释成非页错误的故障地址。"
msgstr ""
"Diagnostics include the exception and error code, RIP/RSP/RFLAGS, segment/control registers, page-"
"fault interpretation, available general-purpose registers, CPU/APIC, the number of other CPUs "
"stopped, task/PID, kernel version, and build identity. Values not saved at entry are explicitly "
"marked unavailable; stale CR2 is not interpreted as a fault address for a non-page-fault "
"exception."

msgid "紧急路径"
msgstr "Emergency Path"

msgid ""
"关闭本地中断，向其他在线 CPU 发送 NMI，并有界等待；绕过普通控制台、 驱动和显卡锁及动态分配。设备或内存损坏时只能尽力输出，保留串口证据。 "
"不自动重启，也不无界遍历可能损坏的栈链。用同一构建调试符号解析指令地址。 用户态异常按其信号/调度策略处理，不把所有用户错误提升为内核 panic。"
msgstr ""
"Local interrupts are disabled, NMIs are sent to other online CPUs, and waiting is bounded. Normal "
"console, driver, and graphics locks and dynamic allocation are bypassed. If devices or memory are "
"damaged, output is best effort, with serial evidence retained. There is no automatic reboot or "
"unbounded traversal of potentially corrupted stack chains. Resolve instruction addresses using "
"debug symbols from the same build. Userspace exceptions follow their signal/scheduling policies; "
"not every user error is escalated to a kernel panic."
